sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-027: Administrative Account Enforcement — Suspension Sequence
    actor Admin
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant AccountService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant FirebaseAuth
    participant ProtectedAPI

    Admin->>ReactUI: Search and inspect account
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/admin/accounts and /:accountId
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify token, MFA, active account, and stored ADMIN role
    alt Visitor, PART, suspended ADMIN, or forged role
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 401 or 403 with no data mutation
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Access denied or retry state
    else Authorized ADMIN
        ExpressAPI->>PostgreSQL: Read safe account, profile, and team listing projection
        PostgreSQL-->>ReactUI: Identifier, role, state, and permitted listing metadata
    end

    Admin->>ReactUI: Submit suspension with mandatory reason
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/admin/accounts/:accountId/suspend
    ExpressAPI->>AccountService: Reject self-suspend, invalid target, or invalid reason
    AccountService->>PostgreSQL: Set is_suspended, timestamp, actor, and reason
    AccountService->>FirebaseAuth: Revoke refresh tokens
    FirebaseAuth-->>AccountService: Sessions revoked or failure
    AccountService->>FirebaseAuth: Disable Firebase user
    FirebaseAuth-->>AccountService: Sign-in disabled or failure
    alt Firebase enforcement fails
        AccountService-->>ReactUI: 502 retry guidance
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Preserve reason and show partial-failure warning
    else Firebase enforcement succeeds
        AccountService->>PostgreSQL: Cancel target pending applications and invitations
        AccountService->>PostgreSQL: Hide profile and clear platform LFT status
        AccountService->>PostgreSQL: Hide owned unlocked Open teams and cancel outgoing invitations
        AccountService->>PostgreSQL: Append safe account_suspend action record
        PostgreSQL-->>AccountService: Cascade counts and audit record ID
        AccountService-->>ReactUI: 200 Suspended with explicit effects
        ReactUI-->>Admin: Show revoked access and preserved memberships
    end

    ProtectedAPI->>PostgreSQL: Recheck participant on protected request
    PostgreSQL-->>ProtectedAPI: Suspended or deactivated flag
    ProtectedAPI-->>ReactUI: 403 ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED

    Note over AccountService,PostgreSQL: Suspension flags, Firebase calls, cascade updates, and audit insertion are sequential, not one atomic transaction. A later failure can leave partial enforcement state.
    Note over FirebaseAuth,ProtectedAPI: Firebase disable blocks new sign-in, token revocation invalidates refresh/session renewal, and requireActiveAccount provides a database-side protected-route backstop.
    Note over ReactUI,AccountService: No unsuspend/reactivate endpoint or Firebase re-enable path is implemented, although the current story description mentions reactivation.

